
  <sn><md>### Factors Affecting Plant Growth

There are several factors that affect plant growth. Specialists have identified **52 factors** that influence plant growth. Some of these include:

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20Fertility/assets/factor-affecting-plant-growth-diagram.png)

:::.row
:::.col-6
- Organic matter of the soil
- Clay
- CEC (Cation Exchange Capacity)
- Moisture
- Relative humidity
- Temperature
- Irrigation
- Drainage
- Latitude
- Altitude
:::

:::.col-6
- Water percolation rate
- Soil water availability
- Evaporation / Transpiration rate
- Present sunshine
- Quality and intensity of light
- Slope and topography
- Depth of root zone
- Manure
- Aeration factor
- Days over 90°F
- Specified crop growth characteristics, etc.
:::
:::
</md></sn>
